Secret files for deploy/compose. This README is tracked. Every other file
in this directory is gitignored.

Create one file per secret, mode 0400, one line, no quotes:

    umask 077
    openssl rand -hex 32 > mcp_unifi_token
    chmod 400 mcp_unifi_token

Files the HTTP compose file mounts:

    mcp_unifi_token       Bearer token clients send as Authorization: Bearer.
                          Generate with openssl rand -hex 32. Not a UniFi key.
    unifi_api_key_home    View-only API key for the controller named home.
    unifi_api_key_cabin   View-only API key for the controller named cabin.

The stdio compose file mounts the API key files and does not mount the
bearer token. Stdio has no HTTP auth.

Docker reads these files as root on the host and mounts them at
/run/secrets/<filename> inside the container. The server reads them once
at startup (MCP_UNIFI_AUTH_TOKEN_FILE and each controller's api_key_file)
and strips a trailing newline. A missing or empty file fails startup.

Do not export these values. Do not copy them into .env, controllers.yaml,
or a compose `environment:` entry. Do not commit them.

How to mint the UniFi key is in README.md under "View-only admin and API key".
